ASSESSMENT

Primary Diagnosis: Internalized Homophobia - Adjustment Disorder - V62.89 (Target of perceived adverse discrimination) - Status: Exacerbated
Differentials:

Acute Gastroenteritis / Food Poisoning - Ruled out/unlikely due to the sudden onset precisely linked to a major psychological trigger, the prominent hyperventilation/spasms, and the absence of diarrhea or fever.

Acute Pancreatitis / Biliary Colic - Ruled out/unlikely as the abdomen is soft without focal, severe tenderness radiating to the back, and the pain is explicitly described as cramping from retching rather than deep visceral pain.

Panic Disorder - Ruled out/unlikely as the primary diagnosis because the severe panic and somatic symptoms are strictly context-dependent, triggered exclusively by the imminent exposure of their marginalized identity, rather than spontaneous occurrences.
